<p:sld xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""/><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="2" name="TextBox 1"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{C2CFA5FB-3FFF-4200-958F-EE54B95DDD40}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="504001" y="1022490"/><a:ext cx="11186475" cy="4985980"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" lIns="0" tIns="0" rIns="0" bIns="0" rtlCol="0"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr marL="285750" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>Review 98 custom code objects which are reported to have pre-existing issues. These pre-existing issues are of 2 types:-</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>With syntax error – means the custom code program has a pre-existing syntax error and can’t be activated in the current ECC system.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>With inconsistent statements – means there is no syntax error in the custom code program, but there are some code lines which if executed will result in a short dump. Currently these issues might not be observed, as these inconsistent statements might be guarded with some conditional blocks which are never executed. In case the business team isn’t facing concerns in the productive environment, these can be ignored too.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:endParaRPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="285750" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>Review 563 custom code objects which involves deprecated functionalities, for example:-</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>Credit management changes in FI/SD</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>GENERAL LEDGER: INCOMPATIBLE CHANGES IN S/4HANA COMPARED TO CLASSIC ERP RELEASES</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:endParaRPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="285750" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>Review 9246 clone programs :</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>A clone programs is a copy of standard SAP object.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>Categories “Very Similar Source Code” and “Identical Source Code” are highlighted to the customer for which the SAP standard object can be adopted with any necessary enhancements done, based on the customization requirements.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>This also helps the customer to cleanse their system and adopt usage of standard processes.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>SAP doesn’t recommends usage of clone objects, thus any remediation / adjustment to the clone objects is kept out of scope.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>Analyze the additional code added in clone objects (as compared to respective standard program), and enhance the standard code going forward in S/4HANA to meet the business requirements.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1100" kern="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>3454 </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>clone objects are impacted and reported as part of ATC report.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:endParaRPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="285750" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>A usage statistics (ST03N / SCMON / UPL) report can help in reducing the custom code footprint in the S/4HANA system. For instance, if a custom code program is not required, then it can be decommissioned.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>Alternatively the usage statistics report can also help in prioritizing the remediations of custom code (as reported in the ATC scans).</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="830138" lvl="1" indent="-285750" fontAlgn="base"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="400"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcAft><a:buClr><a:srgbClr val="0070F2"/></a:buClr><a:buSzPct val="80000"/><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-IN" sz="1100" kern="0" dirty="0"><a:ea typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/><a:cs typeface="Arial Unicode MS" pitchFamily="34" charset="-128"/></a:rPr><a:t>The usage statistics is a good to have report.</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="24" name="Title"/><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="title"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr bwMode="gray"/><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr algn="ctr"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="accent1"/></a:solidFill></a:rPr><a:t>Key Take Away / Next Action Steps</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree><p:custDataLst><p:custData r:id="rId1"/><p:custData r:id="rId2"/></p:custDataLst><p:extLst><p:ext uri="{BB962C8B-B14F-4D97-AF65-F5344CB8AC3E}"><p14:creationId xmlns:p14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/powerpoint/2010/main" val="340897553"/></p:ext></p:extLst></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr></p:sld>